menu "WIFI 8711 (SPI slave transport) module"

config WIFI_8711
	bool "External 8711 Wi-Fi chip over SPI"
	default n
	help
	  Enable the SPI link toward the external 8711FA Wi-Fi chip: the SPI
	  slave transport plus the JPGS/ATMC slot engine.  TCP/IP and the SoftAP
	  live in the 8711's own firmware, so this brings up no Zephyr net stack.

	  Turned on by the wifi_8711 snippet
	  (applications/eBadge_8773g_8711f/snippets/wifi_8711), which also
	  supplies the spi0_slave / wifi_8711_resources / psram1_nc devicetree
	  nodes this module binds to.  Enabling the symbol on its own will not
	  build -- the DT nodes must come with it.

config WIFI_8711_ROLE_SLAVE
	bool "SPI slave role"
	depends on WIFI_8711
	select SPI
	select SPI_SLAVE
	default y
	help
	  Build the SPI slave side: the 8711 drives SCLK and CS, we park a
	  4096-byte slot in TX DMA and wait to be clocked.  This is the only role
	  the v2.0 protocol allows (note/refer/spi-at-command-protocol 1.md
	  sec.1) -- the 8773G cannot generate a clock at all, so there is no
	  master variant to fall back to.  Keep it enabled.

config WIFI_8711_TEST
	bool "wifi8711 shell command group"
	depends on WIFI_8711 && SHELL
	default n
	help
	  Register the `wifi8711` shell commands for bring-up: probe the DT
	  bindings, drive the B2W line, and read W2B.  Useful before the eBadge
	  port_softap / port_tcp layers exist.

endmenu
